      "curator_note": "Table 8.2, row 8: OE+. radical-site displacement 'rd' with RING formation. The Cl+. radical site attacks a distal carbon, forming a cyclic (5-membered) chloronium ion and expelling R.. Book draws 2 arcs -- the Cl-radical hook (odd electron -> forming the new Cl-C bond) and the big arc pulling one C-R electron into that new bond; the third hook (the other C-R electron -> departing R.) is an implicit homolysis hook, not drawn. All 3 encoded. Generic ((CH2)3, CH2R); instantiated R=CH3 (1-chloropentane) -> tetramethylene-chloronium C4H8Cl+ (m/z 91) + .CH3. No m/z / intensity printed."
